content.text:
Opening one section closing another usually doesn't stop a single capture. Many accordions only hide the closed sections, and the text stays in the page. Check that first: if it's true, one copy per page captures everything. If not, a console script can open each section in turn and save them all into one file.

I couldn't test either script, because HDB blocks me (HTTP 403). The selectors are written for standard accessible accordions, so you may need to adjust them.

### Step 1: Check whether closed sections are still in the page (read-only, per page)

Paste this in DevTools → Console. It doesn't click anything.

```js
(() => {
  const main = document.querySelector('main') || document.body;
  const btns = [...main.querySelectorAll('[aria-expanded]')];
  console.table(btns.map((b, i) => {
    const id = b.getAttribute('aria-controls');
    const panel = id ? document.getElementById(id) : b.nextElementSibling;
    return { i, heading: b.textContent.trim().slice(0, 60), expanded: b.getAttribute('aria-expanded'),
             panelInDom: !!panel, panelTextLen: panel ? panel.textContent.trim().length : 0 };
  }));
  const nd = document.getElementById('__NEXT_DATA__');
  console.log('controls:', btns.length, '| <details>:', main.querySelectorAll('details').length,
              '| __NEXT_DATA__ chars:', nd ? nd.textContent.length : 'absent');
})();
```

How to read the output:
- **Every row has `panelTextLen` > 0, including collapsed ones:** the content is in the page. One `copy(document.documentElement.outerHTML)` per page is complete, and you're done.
- **Collapsed rows show 0 or `panelInDom: false`:** those sections are removed from the page while closed. Go to step 2.
- **`controls: 0`:** the accordions don't use standard attributes. Send me the output and I'll adapt the selectors.
- **`__NEXT_DATA__` present and large:** the site may embed all page content as JSON, closed sections included. It's captured by the same copy, and I'll use it offline as a cross-check.

The output contains only headings and counts, so you can paste it back to me without sharing source text.

### Step 2 (only if needed): Collect sections one at a time

This script opens each section in turn, about one per second. It saves each heading and section into one file together with the full page. It also opens parent sections first, so nested accordions are reached.

```js
(async () => {
  const sleep = ms => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));
  const main = document.querySelector('main') || document.body;
  const panelOf = b => { const id = b.getAttribute('aria-controls');
                         return id ? document.getElementById(id) : b.nextElementSibling; };
  const openAncestors = async b => {           // nested accordions: reopen the parent first
    for (const p of [...main.querySelectorAll('[aria-expanded="false"]')])
      if (p !== b && panelOf(p)?.contains(b)) { p.click(); await sleep(1000); }
  };
  const seen = new Set(), sections = [];
  for (let pass = 0, found = true; found && pass < 5; pass++) {   // re-scan for nested ones
    found = false;
    for (const b of [...main.querySelectorAll('[aria-expanded]')]) {
      const key = b.id || b.textContent.trim();
      if (seen.has(key)) continue; seen.add(key); found = true;
      await openAncestors(b);
      if (b.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true') { b.click(); await sleep(1000); }
      const panel = panelOf(b);
      sections.push({ order: sections.length, heading: b.textContent.trim(),
                      expanded: b.getAttribute('aria-expanded'), panel_html: panel ? panel.outerHTML : null });
    }
  }
  copy(JSON.stringify({ url: location.href, captured_at: new Date().toISOString(),
                        user_agent: navigator.userAgent, page_html: document.documentElement.outerHTML, sections }));
  console.log('sections:', sections.length, '| empty:', sections.filter(s => !s.panel_html?.trim()).length,
              '| not expanded:', sections.filter(s => s.expanded !== 'true').length);
})();
```

Save the copied result as `data/private_corpus/raw/S0n/<UTC timestamp>.json`.

The capture is complete when:
- the section count equals the control count from step 1;
- the empty count is 0;
- the not-expanded count is 0.

If any count is off, send me the console line. It contains only numbers.

### Why this approach
- **It's still manual capture.** The script runs in your own normal browser session, at about human clicking speed, on one page you opened yourself. Nothing gets around the bot protection, and nothing follows links. I've recorded it in [plan §10](docs/source_acquisition_plan.md) as manual rendered-DOM capture with sequential console-assisted expansion, so it's disclosed.
- **No images are saved.** The file holds only the page structure: image links and alt text, not the infographic files.
- **Nothing is assembled by hand.** Keeping each section with its own heading avoids misattributing a condition to the wrong applicant group (REQ-SRC-003).
- **Clicking each section and saving separately also works.** It just means about 15 files and is easier to get wrong, so I'd only fall back to it if the script misbehaves.

Once the files are in place, I'll write the offline `register_snapshot.py`. For each file it records the hash and timestamp in the manifest, runs the completeness counts and splits the content into structured passages. It prints only IDs, counts and hashes, never source text.

The HFE page has the same pattern as Couples and Families: every closed section is already in the page, so the procedure stays the same.

| Rows | What they are | Action |
|---|---|---|
| 0–9 | Site navigation (Login, menus) | Ignore |
| 10–13 | Four unlabelled toggles, 31–92 characters each, near the top of the page | Identify them (below) |
| 14 When to apply (1,012 chars) | In the page | Resolves gap G-01, which was missing content |
| 15 How to apply (3,757) | In the page | Contains the HFE steps |
| 16 **Income guidelines (427)** | In the page, but **not in the source-discovery matrix** | I've added it to the plan as S02.g, provisionally Essential. It's probably a short summary pointing to the Income Guidelines page |
| 17 Validity (4,699) | In the page | Contains the validity and review rules |
| 18 Next steps (186) | In the page | Expected to be short, because this section is mostly the journey infographic |

Rows 10–13 have no text label, so they're probably icon buttons. They could be the financial-institution loan note, tabs or slides of the "What is HFE" infographic, or an on-page contents widget. Their content is in the page either way, so it will be captured. I just need to know what they are to label them in the manifest. Run this read-only check, which prints only element attributes and nearby headings:

```js
(() => {
  const btns = [...document.querySelectorAll('[aria-expanded]')].slice(10, 14);
  console.table(btns.map(b => {
    const id = b.getAttribute('aria-controls');
    const panel = id ? document.getElementById(id) : b.nextElementSibling;
    return { tag: b.tagName, cls: String(b.className).slice(0, 50), ariaLabel: b.getAttribute('aria-label'),
             title: b.getAttribute('title'), panelTag: panel?.tagName,
             panelHasImg: !!panel?.querySelector('img'),
             nearHeading: (b.closest('section,div')?.querySelector('h1,h2,h3,h4')?.textContent || '').trim().slice(0, 50) };
  }));
})();
```

Then capture as before:
- **Default copy:** `S02/<UTC timestamp>_default.html`.
- **Expanded copy:** open everything, including rows 10–13 and anything nested inside "How to apply", then save as `S02/<UTC timestamp>_expanded.html`.

About your Couples and Families file: `Couples_families_default.html` is fine, but please rename it to `S01/<UTC timestamp>_default.html` using the time you captured it. The manifest uses that time as the retrieval date, and the file's own modified time could change if the file is copied or edited. I haven't opened the file. Under D-054 option (a), only the offline script will read the captured pages.

Also note any "last updated" date shown on each page.

Once all four pages are captured, I'll run the comparison between the two copies and the checks against the embedded page data.

input.content:
"""Offline completeness audit of manually captured HDB page snapshots (Phase 2a).

Reads the private snapshots in data/private_corpus/raw/S0n/ and prints **structure only**:
headings, accordion labels, presence checks for expected MVP concepts, embedded-data
coverage and hashes. It never prints passages of source text. Under D-054, source text must
not reach an external LLM, and this output is meant to be safe to share with the coding agent.

Stdlib only (D-036). Not used by the app or Docker (REQ-DAT-022).

Usage: python -I scripts/audit_snapshots.py [data/private_corpus/raw]
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import json
import re
import sys
from html.parser import HTMLParser
from pathlib import Path

SKIP_TAGS = {"script", "style", "noscript", "svg", "template"}
HEADING_TAGS = {"h1", "h2", "h3", "h4", "h5", "h6"}
LABEL_MAX = 70  # truncate labels so no passage-length text is ever printed

# Expected MVP concepts per source (plan §2, §5). Regexes over lower-cased page text. A hit
# shows the concept is present in the capture; it does not verify any policy content.
EXPECTED: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {
    "S01": {
        "fiance_section": r"fianc[ée] and fianc[ée]e",
        "married_couples_section": r"married couples?",
        "non_resident_section": r"families with non-residents?|non-resident spouse",
        "ft_pmc": r"first-timer \(parents ?& ?married couples\)|ft\(pmc\)",
        "fpps": r"family and parenthood priority scheme|\bfpps\b",
        "under_21_note": r"below 21|under 21|younger than 21",
        "core_occupier": r"core occupier",
        "application_validity_note": r"no changes? to the persons|changes? to the (persons|applicants|household)",
        "first_timer_term": r"first-timer|first timer",
        "private_property": r"private property|private residential property",
        "citizenship_sc_spr": r"singapore permanent resident|\bspr\b",
        "citizen_top_up_link": r"citizen top-up",
        "income_ceiling_present_excluded": r"income ceiling",
    },
    "S02": {
        "what_is_hfe": r"what is the hdb flat eligibility|what is the hfe",
        "when_to_apply": r"when to apply",
        "how_to_apply": r"how to apply",
        "validity_review": r"validity",
        "next_steps": r"next steps",
        "income_guidelines_section": r"income guidelines",
        "validity_9_months": r"\b9 months\b|nine months",
        "step_window_30_days": r"30 (calendar )?days",
        "processing_time": r"\b1 month\b|one month|processing time|working days",
        "preliminary_hfe": r"preliminary",
        "singpass": r"singpass",
        "ipa": r"in-principle approval|\bipa\b",
        "private_property_declaration": r"private property",
        "review_of_letter": r"review",
    },
    "S03": {
        "supporting_documents": r"supporting documents?",
        "assessment_period": r"assessment period|12 months|preceding",
        "employed": r"\bemployed\b",
        "self_employed": r"self-employed",
        "not_working": r"not working|unemployed",
        "payslip_or_cpf": r"payslip|cpf contribution|cpf statement",
        "employment_status_guide_link": r"employment status guide",
        "income_declaration_guide_link": r"income declaration guide",
    },
    "S04": {
        "cancellation_section": r"cancel",
        "non_selection": r"non-selection|not (to )?select|do not book|did not book|not book a flat",
        "waiver": r"waive",
        "exception": r"exception",
        "first_timer_term": r"first-timer|first timer",
        "valid_hfe_required": r"hfe letter",
        "sales_launch": r"sales launch|sales exercise",
        "ballot": r"ballot",
        "application_fee": r"application fee|administrative fee|\$10\b",
        "priority_schemes_link": r"priority scheme",
    },
}
LINK_PATTERNS = {
    "file.go.gov.sg PDFs": r"file\.go\.gov\.sg",
    "mynicehome guide": r"mynicehome",
    "youtube": r"youtu\.?be",
    "hfe get-help (robots-disallowed)": r"hdb-flat-portal/hfe/get-help",
    "income-guidelines page": r"income-guidelines-and-documents",
    "priority-schemes page": r"priority-schemes",
    "citizen-topup": r"citizen-topup",
}
UPDATED_RE = re.compile(r"(last updated|updated on|last reviewed)[^0-9a-z]{0,5}([0-9a-z ,]{4,25})")


def norm(s: str) -> str:
    return re.sub(r"\s+", " ", s.replace("\xa0", " ")).strip().lower()


class Snapshot(HTMLParser):
    """Collects visible-DOM text, headings, toggles, links, images and __NEXT_DATA__."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)
        self.text: list[str] = []
        self.headings: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        self.toggles: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        self.links: list[str] = []
        self.images: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        self.next_data = ""
        self.title = ""
        self._skip = 0
        self._in_next = False
        self._in_title = False
        self._label_stack: list[tuple[str, str, list[str]]] = []  # (kind, tag, parts)

    def handle_starttag(self, tag: str, attrs: list[tuple[str, str | None]]) -> None:
        a = {k: v or "" for k, v in attrs}
        if tag == "script" and a.get("id") == "__NEXT_DATA__":
            self._in_next = True
        if tag in SKIP_TAGS:
            self._skip += 1
            return
        if tag == "title":
            self._in_title = True
        if tag in HEADING_TAGS:
            self._label_stack.append(("h", tag, []))
        elif "aria-expanded" in a:
            self._label_stack.append(("t", tag, [a.get("aria-expanded", "")]))
        if tag == "a" and a.get("href"):
            self.links.append(a["href"])
        if tag == "img":
            self.images.append((a.get("src", ""), a.get("alt", "")))

    def handle_endtag(self, tag: str) -> None:
        if tag == "script":
            self._in_next = False
        if tag in SKIP_TAGS:
            self._skip = max(0, self._skip - 1)
            return
        if tag == "title":
            self._in_title = False
        if self._label_stack and self._label_stack[-1][1] == tag:
            kind, t, parts = self._label_stack.pop()
            if kind == "h":
                self.headings.append((t, norm(" ".join(parts))))
            else:
                self.toggles.append((parts[0], norm(" ".join(parts[1:]))))

    def handle_data(self, data: str) -> None:
        if self._in_next:
            self.next_data += data
            return
        if self._skip:
            return
        if self._in_title:
            self.title += data
        self.text.append(data)
        for _, _, parts in self._label_stack:
            parts.append(data)


class _Strip(HTMLParser):
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True)
        self.parts: list[str] = []

    def handle_data(self, data: str) -> None:
        self.parts.append(data)


def strip_html(s: str) -> str:
    p = _Strip()
    p.feed(s)
    return " ".join(p.parts)


def json_strings(node: object, path: str = "$") -> list[tuple[str, str]]:
    out: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
    if isinstance(node, dict):
        for k, v in node.items():
            out += json_strings(v, f"{path}.{k}")
    elif isinstance(node, list):
        for i, v in enumerate(node):
            out += json_strings(v, f"{path}[{i}]")
    elif isinstance(node, str):
        out.append((path, node))
    return out


def next_data_coverage(raw: str, dom: str) -> tuple[int, int, list[tuple[str, int]]]:
    """Share of content sentences in __NEXT_DATA__ that also appear in the DOM text.

    A sentence missing from the DOM means content that exists in page data but was not
    rendered at capture (e.g. unmounted panels). Returns (total, found, missing paths)."""
    if not raw.strip():
        return 0, 0, []
    total = found = 0
    missing: dict[str, int] = {}
    for path, s in json_strings(json.loads(raw)):
        if len(s) < 40 or s.startswith(("http", "/", "{")):
            continue
        txt = norm(strip_html(s) if "<" in s else s)
        for sent in re.split(r"(?<=[.!?:;])\s+", txt):
            if len(sent) < 30:
                continue
            total += 1
            if sent in dom:
                found += 1
            else:
                missing[path] = missing.get(path, 0) + 1
    return total, found, sorted(missing.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])


def short(s: str) -> str:
    return s if len(s) <= LABEL_MAX else s[: LABEL_MAX - 1] + "…"


def audit(path: Path, source_id: str) -> None:
    data = path.read_bytes()
    snap = Snapshot()
    snap.feed(data.decode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
    dom = norm(" ".join(snap.text))
    print(f"\n=== {source_id}: {path.name}")
    print(f"bytes={len(data)} sha256={hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()}")
    print(f"text_sha256={hashlib.sha256(dom.encode()).hexdigest()} dom_text_chars={len(dom)}")
    print(f"title: {short(norm(snap.title))}")
    m = UPDATED_RE.search(dom)
    print(f"last-updated marker: {m.group(0) if m else 'none found'}")

    print(f"headings ({len(snap.headings)}):")
    for tag, h in snap.headings:
        if h:
            print(f"  {tag}: {short(h)}")
    print(f"toggles with aria-expanded ({len(snap.toggles)}):")
    for state, label in snap.toggles:
        print(f"  [{state}] {short(label) or '(no text label)'}")

    print("expected concepts:")
    hits = 0
    for name, rx in EXPECTED.get(source_id, {}).items():
        n = len(re.findall(rx, dom))
        hits += n > 0
        print(f"  {'OK ' if n else 'MISSING'} {name} (matches={n})")
    print(f"  -> {hits}/{len(EXPECTED.get(source_id, {}))} present")

    print("links of interest:")
    for name, rx in LINK_PATTERNS.items():
        n = sum(bool(re.search(rx, h)) for h in snap.links)
        if n:
            print(f"  {name}: {n}")
    content_imgs = [(s, a) for s, a in snap.images if "/-/media/" in s or "infographic" in s.lower()]
    print(f"content images ({len(content_imgs)}):")
    for src, alt in content_imgs:
        print(f"  {short(src.split('?')[0].rsplit('/', 1)[-1])} | alt_chars={len(alt)}")

    total, found, missing = next_data_coverage(snap.next_data, dom)
    print(f"__NEXT_DATA__ sentences rendered in DOM: {found}/{total}")
    for p, n in missing[:15]:
        print(f"  not in DOM: {n} sentence(s) at {short(p)}")


def main() -> None:
    root = Path(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "data/private_corpus/raw")
    for sid in sorted(EXPECTED):
        for f in sorted((root / sid).glob("*.html")):
            audit(f, sid)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()

